{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lesley Gore fits the '60s pop listening reflected in AM Gold and my other oldies collections; those songs feel like a natural next choice.",
    "Carole King's melodic songwriting connects with what draws me to Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie, while Songs in the Key of Life also appeals through its rich melodies and classic songs."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "At Folsom Prison, Need You Now, and Toby Keith's collection miss what I want today: melodic older pop and folk. Being familiar recordings or hits collections does not make country music an equally close match.",
    "Survivor and Pat Benatar connect with my classic rock listening, but their more energetic sound is less appealing right now than the softer oldies selections. I also cannot judge Greatest Hits without knowing the artist."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to put too much weight on my interest in greatest-hits collections, even when the music itself differs from what I want.",
    "My Cars and classic rock listening seems to have been taken as a broad preference for energetic rock, although that is only one part of my listening."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection among Simon & Garfunkel, Melanie, and my '60s compilations matters because I am drawn to melodic songs and folk-influenced pop.",
    "A recording can fit my broader taste without being something I would choose today; I currently favor softer oldies over harder rock or country."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in classic recordings and compilations but only partly captured my current preference for melodic oldies and folk-pop."
}"}
